  "question": {
    "text": "The rate law for the reaction below is given by the expression <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>]</mo></math><br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math><br /><br />If the concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is increased from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>to</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></math>, keeping the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></math>, the rate constant will be:"
